INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('1KI',  22,  38, 'They washed the chariot by the pool of Samaria; and the dogs licked up his blood where the prostitutes washed themselves; according to the word of ForeverOne which he spoke.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('1KI',  22,  38, 'They washed the chariot by the pool of Samaria; and the dogs licked up his blood where the prostitutes washed themselves, according to ForeverOne\'s word which he spoke.');
-
-
-
-
-
-
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('1KI',  22,  43, 'He walked in all the way of Asa his father; He didn\'t turn aside from it, doing that which was right in the eyes of ForeverOne: however the high places were not taken away; the people still sacrificed and burnt incense in the high places.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('1KI',  22,  43, 'He walked in all the way of Asa his father. He didn\'t turn away from it, doing that which was right in ForeverOne\'s eyes. However, the high places were not taken away. The people still sacrificed and burned incense on the high places.');
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('1KI',  22,  45, 'Now the rest of the acts of Jehoshaphat, and his might that he showed, and how he warred, aren\'t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('1KI',  22,  45, 'Now the rest of the acts of Jehoshaphat, and his might that he showed, and how he fought, aren\'t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?');
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('1KI',  22,  47, 'There was no king in Edom: a deputy was king.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('1KI',  22,  47, 'There was no king in Edom. A deputy ruled.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('1KI',  22,  48, 'Jehoshaphat made ships of Tarshish to go to Ophir for gold: but they didn\'t go; for the ships were broken at Ezion Geber.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('1KI',  22,  48, 'Jehoshaphat made ships of Tarshish to go to Ophir for gold, but they didn\'t go, for the ships wrecked at Ezion Geber.');
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('1KI',  22,  50, 'Jehoshaphat slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in the city of David his father; Jehoram his son reigned in his place.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('1KI',  22,  50, 'Jehoshaphat slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in his father David\'s city. Jehoram his son reigned in his place.');
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('1KI',  22,  52, 'He did that which was evil in the sight of ForeverOne, and walked in the way of his father, and in the way of his mother, and in the way of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, in which he made Israel to sin.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('1KI',  22,  52, 'He did that which was evil in ForeverOne\'s sight, and walked in the way of his father, and in the way of his mother, and in the way of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, in which he made Israel to sin.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('1KI',  22,  53, 'He served Baal, and worshiped him, and provoked to anger ForeverOne, the God of Israel, according to all that his father had done.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('1KI',  22,  53, 'He served Baal and worshiped him, and provoked ForeverOne, the God of Israel, to anger in all the ways that his father had done so.');
-
-
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   1,   3, 'But the angel of ForeverOne said to Elijah the Tishbite, \"Arise, go up to meet the messengers of the king of Samaria, and tell them, \'Is it because there is no God in Israel, that you go to inquire of Baal Zebub, the god of Ekron?');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   1,   3, 'But ForeverOne\'s angel said to Elijah the Tishbite, \"Arise, go up to meet the messengers of the king of Samaria, and tell them, \'Is it because there is no God in Israel that you go to inquire of Baal Zebub, the god of Ekron?');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   1,   4, 'Now therefore thus says ForeverOne, \"You shall not come down from the bed where you have gone up, but shall surely die.\"\'\" Elijah departed.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   1,   4, 'Now therefore ForeverOne says, \"You will not come down from the bed where you have gone up, but you will surely die.\"\'\" Then Elijah departed.');
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   1,   6, 'They said to him, \"A man came up to meet us, and said to us, \'Go, return to the king who sent you, and tell him, \"Thus says ForeverOne, \'Is it because there is no God in Israel, that you send to inquire of Baal Zebub, the god of Ekron? Therefore you shall not come down from the bed where you have gone up, but shall surely die.\'\"\'\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   1,   6, 'They said to him, \"A man came up to meet us, and said to us, \'Go, return to the king who sent you, and tell him, \"ForeverOne says, \'Is it because there is no God in Israel that you send to inquire of Baal Zebub, the god of Ekron? Therefore you will not come down from the bed where you have gone up, but you will surely die.\'\"\'\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   1,   7, 'He said to them, \"What kind of man was he who came up to meet you, and told you these words?\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   1,   7, 'He said to them, \"What kind of man was he who came up to meet you and told you these words?\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   1,   8, 'They answered him, \"He was a hairy man, and wearing a leather belt around his waist.\" He said, \"It is Elijah the Tishbite.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   1,   8, 'They answered him, \"He was a hairy man, and wearing a leather belt around his waist.\" He said, \"It\'s Elijah the Tishbite.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   1,   9, 'Then [the king] sent a captain of fifty with his fifty to him. He went up to him; and behold, he was sitting on the top of the hill. He said to him, \"Man of God, the king has said, \'Come down!\'\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   1,   9, 'Then the king sent a captain of fifty with his fifty to him. He went up to him; and behold, he was sitting on the top of the hill. He said to him, \"Man of God, the king has said, \'Come down!\'\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   1,  10, 'Elijah answered to the captain of fifty, \"If I am a man of God, let fire come down from the sky, and consume you and your fifty!\" Fire came down from the sky, and consumed him and his fifty.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   1,  10, 'Elijah answered to the captain of fifty, \"If I am a man of God, then let fire come down from the sky and consume you and your fifty!\" Then fire came down from the sky, and consumed him and his fifty.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   1,  11, 'Again he sent to him another captain of fifty and his fifty. He answered him, \"Man of God, the king has said, \'Come down quickly!\'\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   1,  11, 'Again he sent to him another captain of fifty with his fifty. He answered him, \"Man of God, the king has said, \'Come down quickly!\'\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   1,  12, 'Elijah answered them, \"If I am a man of God, let fire come down from the sky, and consume you and your fifty!\" The fire of God came down from the sky, and consumed him and his fifty.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   1,  12, 'Elijah answered them, \"If I am a man of God, then let fire come down from the sky and consume you and your fifty!\" Then God\'s fire came down from the sky, and consumed him and his fifty.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   1,  13, 'Again he sent the captain of a third fifty with his fifty. The third captain of fifty went up, and came and fell on his knees before Elijah, and begged him, and said to him, \"Man of God, please let my life, and the life of these fifty your servants, be precious in your sight.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   1,  13, 'Again he sent the captain of a third fifty with his fifty. The third captain of fifty went up, and came and fell on his knees before Elijah, and begged him, and said to him, \"Man of God, please let my life and the life of these fifty of your servants be precious in your sight.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   1,  14, 'Behold, fire came down from the sky, and consumed the two former captains of fifty with their fifties. But now let my life be precious in your sight.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   1,  14, 'Behold, fire came down from the sky and consumed the last two captains of fifty with their fifties. But now let my life be precious in your sight.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   1,  15, 'The angel of ForeverOne said to Elijah, \"Go down with him. Don\'t be afraid of him.\" He arose, and went down with him to the king.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   1,  15, 'ForeverOne\'s angel said to Elijah, \"Go down with him. Don\'t be afraid of him.\" Then he arose and went down with him to the king.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   1,  16, 'He said to him, \"Thus says ForeverOne, \'Because you have sent messengers to inquire of Baal Zebub, the god of Ekron, is it because there is no God in Israel to inquire of his word? Therefore you shall not come down from the bed where you have gone up, but shall surely die.\'\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   1,  16, 'He said to him, \"ForeverOne says, \'Because you have sent messengers to inquire of Baal Zebub, the god of Ekron, is it because there is no God in Israel to inquire of his word? Therefore you will not come down from the bed where you have gone up, but you will surely die.\'\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   1,  17, 'So he died according to the word of ForeverOne which Elijah had spoken. Jehoram began to reign in his place in the second year of Jehoram the son of Jehoshaphat king of Judah; because he had no son.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   1,  17, 'So he died according to ForeverOne\'s word which Elijah had spoken. Jehoram began to reign in his place in the second year of Jehoram the son of Jehoshaphat king of Judah, because he had no son.');
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,   1, 'It happened, when ForeverOne would take up Elijah by a whirlwind into heaven, that Elijah went with Elisha from Gilgal.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,   1, 'When ForeverOne was about to take Elijah up by a whirlwind into heaven, Elijah went with Elisha from Gilgal.');
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,   3, 'The sons of the prophets who were at Bethel came out to Elisha, and said to him, \"Do you know that ForeverOne will take away your master from your head today?\" He said, \"Yes, I know it; hold your peace.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,   3, 'The sons of the prophets who were at Bethel came out to Elisha, and said to him, \"Do you know that ForeverOne will take away your master from over you today?\" He said, \"Yes, I know it. Hold your peace.\"');
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,   5, 'The sons of the prophets who were at Jericho came near to Elisha, and said to him, \"Do you know that ForeverOne will take away your master from your head today?\" He answered, \"Yes, I know it. Hold your peace.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,   5, 'The sons of the prophets who were at Jericho came near to Elisha, and said to him, \"Do you know that ForeverOne will take away your master from over you today?\" He answered, \"Yes, I know it. Hold your peace.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,   6, 'Elijah said to him, \"Please wait here, for ForeverOne has sent me to the Jordan.\" He said, \"As ForeverOne lives, and as your soul lives, I will not leave you.\" They both went on.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,   6, 'Elijah said to him, \"Please wait here, for ForeverOne has sent me to the Jordan.\" He said, \"As ForeverOne lives, and as your soul lives, I will not leave you.\" Then they both went on.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,   7, 'Fifty men of the sons of the prophets went, and stood opposite them at a distance; and they both stood by the Jordan.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,   7, 'Fifty men of the sons of the prophets went and stood opposite them at a distance; and they both stood by the Jordan.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,   8, 'Elijah took his mantle, and wrapped it together, and struck the waters, and they were divided here and there, so that they two went over on dry ground.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,   8, 'Elijah took his mantle, and rolled it up, and struck the waters; and they were divided here and there, so that they both went over on dry ground.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,   9, 'It happened, when they had gone over, that Elijah said to Elisha, \"Ask what I shall do for you, before I am taken from you.\" Elisha said, \"Please let a double portion of your spirit be on me.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,   9, 'When they had gone over, Elijah said to Elisha, \"Ask what I shall do for you, before I am taken from you.\" Elisha said, \"Please let a double portion of your spirit be on me.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,  10, 'He said, \"You have asked a hard thing. If you see me when I am taken from you, it shall be so for you; but if not, it shall not be so.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,  10, 'He said, \"You have asked a hard thing. If you see me when I am taken from you, it will be so for you; but if not, it will not be so.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,  11, 'It happened, as they still went on, and talked, that behold, a chariot of fire and horses of fire separated them; and Elijah went up by a whirlwind into heaven.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,  11, 'As they continued on and talked, behold, a chariot of fire and horses of fire separated them; and Elijah went up by a whirlwind into heaven.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,  12, 'Elisha saw it, and he cried, \"My father, my father, the chariots of Israel and its horsemen!\" He saw him no more: and he took hold of his own clothes, and tore them in two pieces.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,  12, 'Elisha saw it, and he cried, \"My father, my father, the chariots of Israel and its horsemen!\" He saw him no more. Then he took hold of his own clothes and tore them in two pieces.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,  13, 'He took up also the mantle of Elijah that fell from him, and went back, and stood by the bank of the Jordan.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,  13, 'He also took up Elijah\'s mantle that fell from him, and went back and stood by the bank of the Jordan.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,  14, 'He took the mantle of Elijah that fell from him, and struck the waters, and said, \"Where is ForeverOne, the God of Elijah?\" When he also had struck the waters, they were divided here and there; and Elisha went over.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,  14, 'He took Elijah\'s mantle that fell from him, and struck the waters, and said, \"Where is ForeverOne, the God of Elijah?\" When he also had struck the waters, they were divided apart, and Elisha went over.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,  15, 'When the sons of the prophets who were at Jericho over against him saw him, they said, \"The spirit of Elijah rests on Elisha.\" They came to meet him, and bowed themselves to the ground before him.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,  15, 'When the sons of the prophets who were at Jericho facing him saw him, they said, \"The spirit of Elijah rests on Elisha.\" They came to meet him, and bowed themselves to the ground before him.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,  16, 'They said to him, \"See now, there are with your servants fifty strong men. Please let them go and seek your master. Perhaps the Spirit of ForeverOne has taken him up, and put him on some mountain, or into some valley. He said, \"You shall not send them.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,  16, 'They said to him, \"See now, there are with your servants fifty strong men. Please let them go and seek your master. Perhaps ForeverOne\'s Spirit has taken him up, and put him on some mountain or into some valley.\" He said, \"Don\'t send them.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,  17, 'When they urged him until he was ashamed, he said, \"Send them.\" They sent therefore fifty men; and they searched for three days, but didn\'t find him.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,  17, 'When they urged him until he was ashamed, he said, \"Send them.\" Therefore they sent fifty men; and they searched for three days, but didn\'t find him.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,  18, 'They came back to him, while he stayed at Jericho; and he said to them, \"Didn\'t I tell you, \'Don\'t go?\'\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,  18, 'They came back to him while he stayed at Jericho; and he said to them, \"Didn\'t I tell you, \'Don\'t go?\'\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,  19, 'The men of the city said to Elisha, \"Behold, please, the situation of this city is pleasant, as my lord sees; but the water is bad, and the land miscarries.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,  19, 'The men of the city said to Elisha, \"Behold, please, the situation of this city is pleasant, as my lord sees; but the water is bad, and the land is barren.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,  20, 'He said, \"Bring me a new jar, and put salt in it.\" They brought it to him.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,  20, 'He said, \"Bring me a new jar, and put salt in it.\" Then they brought it to him.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,  21, 'He went out to the spring of the waters, and threw salt into it, and said, \"Thus says ForeverOne, \'I have healed these waters. There shall not be from there any more death or miscarrying.\'\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,  21, 'He went out to the spring of the waters, and threw salt into it, and said, \"ForeverOne says, \'I have healed these waters. There shall not be from there any more death or barren wasteland.\'\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,  22, 'So the waters were healed to this day, according to the word of Elisha which he spoke.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,  22, 'So the waters were healed to this day, according to Elisha\'s word which he spoke.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,  23, 'He went up from there to Bethel. As he was going up by the way, some youths came out of the city and mocked him, and said to him, \"Go up, you baldy! Go up, you baldhead!\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,  23, 'He went up from there to Bethel. As he was going up by the way, some youths came out of the city and mocked him, and said to him, \"Go up, you baldy! Go up, you baldy!\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,  24, 'He looked behind him and saw them, and cursed them in the name of ForeverOne. Two female bears came out of the woods, and mauled forty-two of those youths.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   2,  24, 'He looked behind him and saw them, and cursed them in ForeverOne\'s name. Then two female bears came out of the woods and mauled forty-two of those youths.');
-
-
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,   2, 'He did that which was evil in the sight of ForeverOne, but not like his father, and like his mother; for he put away the pillar of Baal that his father had made.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,   2, 'He did that which was evil in ForeverOne\'s sight, but not like his father and like his mother, for he put away the pillar of Baal that his father had made.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,   3, 'Nevertheless he held to the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, with which he made Israel to sin; he didn\'t depart from it.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,   3, 'Nevertheless he held to the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, with which he made Israel to sin. He didn\'t depart from them.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,   4, 'Now Mesha king of Moab was a sheep breeder; and he rendered to the king of Israel the wool of one hundred thousand lambs, and of one hundred thousand rams.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,   4, 'Now Mesha king of Moab was a sheep breeder; and he supplied the king of Israel with one hundred thousand lambs and the wool of one hundred thousand rams.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,   5, 'But it happened, when Ahab was dead, that the king of Moab rebelled against the king of Israel.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,   5, 'But when Ahab was dead, the king of Moab rebelled against the king of Israel.');
-
-
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,   8, 'He said, \"Which way shall we go up?\" He answered, \"The way of the wilderness of Edom.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,   8, 'Then he said, \"Which way shall we go up?\" Jehoram answered, \"The way of the wilderness of Edom.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,   9, 'So the king of Israel went, and the king of Judah, and the king of Edom; and they made a circuit of seven days\' journey. There was no water for the army, nor for the animals that followed them.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,   9, 'So the king of Israel went with the king of Judah and the king of Edom, and they marched for seven days along a circuitous route. There was no water for the army or for the animals that followed them.');
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,  11, 'But Jehoshaphat said, \"Isn\'t there here a prophet of ForeverOne, that we may inquire of ForeverOne by him?\" One of the king of Israel\'s servants answered, \"Elisha the son of Shaphat is here, who poured water on the hands of Elijah.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,  11, 'But Jehoshaphat said, \"Isn\'t there a prophet of ForeverOne here, that we may inquire of ForeverOne by him?\" One of the king of Israel\'s servants answered, \"Elisha the son of Shaphat, who poured water on the hands of Elijah, is here.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,  12, 'Jehoshaphat said, \"The word of ForeverOne is with him.\" So the king of Israel and Jehoshaphat and the king of Edom went down to him.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,  12, 'Jehoshaphat said, \"ForeverOne\'s word is with him.\" So the king of Israel and Jehoshaphat and the king of Edom went down to him.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,  13, 'Elisha said to the king of Israel, \"What have I to do with you? Go to the prophets of your father, and to the prophets of your mother.\" The king of Israel said to him, \"No; for ForeverOne has called these three kings together to deliver them into the hand of Moab.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,  13, 'Elisha said to the king of Israel, \"What have I to do with you? Go to the prophets of your father, and to the prophets of your mother.\" The king of Israel said to him, \"No, for ForeverOne has called these three kings together to deliver them into the hand of Moab.\"');
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,  15, 'But now bring me a minstrel.\" It happened, when the minstrel played, that the hand of ForeverOne came on him.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,  15, 'But now bring me a musician.\" When the musician played, ForeverOne\'s hand came on him.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,  16, 'He said, \"Thus says ForeverOne, \'Make this valley full of trenches.\'');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,  16, 'He said, \"ForeverOne says, \'Make this valley full of trenches.\'');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,  17, 'For thus says ForeverOne, \'You will not see wind, neither will you see rain; yet that valley shall be filled with water, and you will drink, both you and your livestock and your animals.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,  17, 'For ForeverOne says, \'You will not see wind, neither will you see rain, yet that valley will be filled with water, and you will drink, both you and your livestock and your other animals.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,  18, 'This is but a light thing in the sight of ForeverOne. He will also deliver the Moabites into your hand.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,  18, 'This is an easy thing in ForeverOne\'s sight. He will also deliver the Moabites into your hand.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,  19, 'You shall strike every fortified city, and every choice city, and shall fell every good tree, and stop all springs of water, and mar every good piece of land with stones.\'\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,  19, 'You shall strike every fortified city and every choice city, and shall fell every good tree, and stop all springs of water, and mar every good piece of land with stones.\'\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,  20, 'It happened in the morning, about the time of offering the offering, that behold, water came by the way of Edom, and the country was filled with water.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,  20, 'In the morning, about the time of offering the sacrifice, behold, water came by the way of Edom, and the country was filled with water.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,  21, 'Now when all the Moabites heard that the kings had come up to fight against them, they gathered themselves together, all who were able to put on armor, and upward, and stood on the border.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,  21, 'Now when all the Moabites heard that the kings had come up to fight against them, they gathered themselves together, all who were able to put on armor, young and old, and stood on the border.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,  22, 'They rose up early in the morning, and the sun shone on the water, and the Moabites saw the water over against them as red as blood.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,  22, 'They rose up early in the morning, and the sun shone on the water, and the Moabites saw the water opposite them as red as blood.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,  23, 'They said, \"This is blood. The kings are surely destroyed, and they have struck each other. Now therefore, Moab, to the spoil!\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,  23, 'They said, \"This is blood. The kings are surely destroyed, and they have struck each other. Now therefore, Moab, to the plunder!\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,  24, 'When they came to the camp of Israel, the Israelites rose up and struck the Moabites, so that they fled before them; and they went forward into the land smiting the Moabites.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,  24, 'When they came to the camp of Israel, the Israelites rose up and struck the Moabites, so that they fled before them; and they went forward into the land attacking the Moabites.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,  25, 'They beat down the cities; and on every good piece of land they cast every man his stone, and filled it; and they stopped all the springs of water, and felled all the good trees, until in Kir Hareseth [only] they left its stones; however the men armed with slings went about it, and struck it.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,  25, 'They beat down the cities; and on every good piece of land each man cast his stone, and filled it. They also stopped all the springs of water and cut down all the good trees, until in Kir Hareseth all they left was its stones; however the men armed with slings went around it and attacked it.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,  26, 'When the king of Moab saw that the battle was too severe for him, he took with him seven hundred men who drew sword, to break through to the king of Edom; but they could not.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,  26, 'When the king of Moab saw that the battle was too severe for him, he took with him seven hundred men who drew a sword, to break through to the king of Edom; but they could not.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,  27, 'Then he took his eldest son who would have reigned in his place, and offered him for a burnt offering on the wall. There was great wrath against Israel: and they departed from him, and returned to their own land.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   3,  27, 'Then he took his oldest son who would have reigned in his place, and offered him for a burnt offering on the wall. There was great wrath against Israel; and they departed from him, and returned to their own land.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,   1, 'Now there cried a certain woman of the wives of the sons of the prophets to Elisha, saying, \"Your servant my husband is dead. You know that your servant feared ForeverOne. Now the creditor has come to take for himself my two children to be slaves.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,   1, 'Now a certain woman of the wives of the sons of the prophets cried out to Elisha, saying, \"Your servant my husband is dead. You know that your servant feared ForeverOne. Now the creditor has come to take for himself my two children to be slaves.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,   2, 'Elisha said to her, \"What shall I do for you? Tell me: what do you have in the house?\" She said, \"Your handmaid has nothing in the house, except a pot of oil.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,   2, 'Elisha said to her, \"What should I do for you? Tell me, what do you have in the house?\" She said, \"Your servant has nothing in the house, except a pot of oil.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,   3, 'Then he said, \"Go, borrow containers from of all your neighbors, even empty containers. Don\'t borrow just a few.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,   3, 'Then he said, \"Go, borrow empty containers from all your neighbors. Don\'t borrow just a few containers.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,   4, 'You shall go in, and shut the door on you and on your sons, and pour out into all those containers; and you shall set aside that which is full.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,   4, 'Go in and shut the door on you and on your sons, and pour oil into all those containers; and set aside those which are full.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,   5, 'So she went from him, and shut the door on her and on her sons; they brought the containers to her, and she poured out.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,   5, 'So she went from him, and shut the door on herself and on her sons. They brought the containers to her, and she poured oil.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,   6, 'It happened, when the containers were full, that she said to her son, \"Bring me another container.\" He said to her, \"There isn\'t another container.\" The oil stopped flowing.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,   6, 'When the containers were full, she said to her son, \"Bring me another container.\" He said to her, \"There isn\'t another container.\" Then the oil stopped flowing.');
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,   8, 'It fell on a day, that Elisha passed to Shunem, where there was a prominent woman; and she persuaded him to eat bread. So it was, that as often as he passed by, he turned in there to eat bread.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,   8, 'One day Elisha went to Shunem, where there was a prominent woman; and she persuaded him to eat bread. So it was, that as often as he passed by, he turned in there to eat bread.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,   9, 'She said to her husband, \"See now, I perceive that this is a holy man of God, that passes by us continually.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,   9, 'She said to her husband, \"See now, I perceive that this is a holy man of God who passes by us continually.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  10, 'Please let us make a little room on the wall. Let us set for him there a bed, a table, a chair, and a lampstand. It shall be, when he comes to us, that he shall turn in there.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  10, 'Please, let\'s make a little room on the roof. Let\'s set a bed, a table, a chair, and a lampstand for him there. When he comes to us, he can stay there.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  11, 'One day he came there, and he turned into the room and lay there.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  11, 'One day he came there, and he went to the room and lay there.');
-
-
-
-
-
-
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  16, 'He said, \"At this season, when the time comes around, you will embrace a son.\" She said, \"No, my lord, you man of God, do not lie to your handmaid.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  16, 'He said, \"At this season next year, you will embrace a son.\" She said, \"No, my lord, you man of God, do not lie to your servant.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  17, 'The woman conceived, and bore a son at that season, when the time came around, as Elisha had said to her.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  17, 'The woman conceived, and bore a son at that season when the time came around, as Elisha had said to her.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  18, 'When the child was grown, it happened one day that he went out to his father to the reapers.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  18, 'When the child was grown, one day he went out to his father to the reapers.');
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  20, 'When he had taken him, and brought him to his mother, he sat on her knees until noon, and then died.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  20, 'When he had taken him and brought him to his mother, he sat on her knees until noon, and then died.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  21, 'She went up and laid him on the bed of the man of God, and shut the door on him, and went out.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  21, 'She went up and laid him on the man of God\'s bed, and shut the door on him, and went out.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  22, 'She called to her husband, and said, \"Please send me one of the servants, and one of the donkeys, that I may run to the man of God, and come again.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  22, 'She called to her husband and said, \"Please send me one of the servants, and one of the donkeys, that I may run to the man of God and come again.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  23, 'He said, \"Why would you want go to him today? It is neither new moon nor Sabbath.\" She said, \"It\'s alright.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  23, 'He said, \"Why would you want go to him today? It is not a new moon or a Sabbath.\" She said, \"It\'s all right.\"');
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  25, 'So she went, and came to the man of God to Mount Carmel. It happened, when the man of God saw her afar off, that he said to Gehazi his servant, \"Behold, there is the Shunammite.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  25, 'So she went, and came to the man of God to Mount Carmel. When the man of God saw her afar off, he said to Gehazi his servant, \"Behold, there is the Shunammite.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  26, 'Please run now to meet her, and ask her, \'Is it well with you? Is it well with your husband? Is it well with the child?\'\" She answered, \"It is well.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  26, 'Please run now to meet her, and ask her, \'Is it well with you? Is it well with your husband? Is it well with your child?\'\" She answered, \"It is well.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  27, 'When she came to the man of God to the hill, she caught hold of his feet. Gehazi came near to thrust her away; but the man of God said, \"Leave her alone; for her soul is troubled within her; and ForeverOne has hidden it from me, and has not told me.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  27, 'When she came to the man of God to the hill, she caught hold of his feet. Gehazi came near to thrust her away; but the man of God said, \"Leave her alone, for her soul is troubled within her; and ForeverOne has hidden it from me, and has not told me.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  28, 'Then she said, \"Did I desire a son of my lord? Didn\'t I say, Do not deceive me?\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  28, 'Then she said, \"Did I ask you for a son, my lord? Didn\'t I say, \'Do not deceive me\'?\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  29, 'Then he said to Gehazi, \"Tuck your cloak into your belt, take my staff in your hand, and go your way. If you meet any man, don\'t greet him; and if anyone greets you, don\'t answer him again. Then lay my staff on the face of the child.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  29, 'Then he said to Gehazi, \"Tuck your cloak into your belt, take my staff in your hand, and go your way. If you meet any man, don\'t greet him; and if anyone greets you, don\'t answer him again. Then lay my staff on the child\'s face.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  30, 'The mother of the child said, \"As ForeverOne lives, and as your soul lives, I will not leave you.\" He arose, and followed her.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  30, 'The child\'s mother said, \"As ForeverOne lives, and as your soul lives, I will not leave you.\" So he arose, and followed her.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  31, 'Gehazi passed on before them, and laid the staff on the face of the child; but there was neither voice, nor hearing. Therefore he returned to meet him, and told him, saying, \"The child has not awakened.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  31, 'Gehazi went ahead of them, and laid the staff on the child\'s face; but there was no voice and no hearing. Therefore he returned to meet him, and told him, \"The child has not awakened.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  32, 'When Elisha had come into the house, behold, the child was dead, and laid on his bed.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  32, 'When Elisha had come into the house, behold, the child was dead, and lying on his bed.');
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  34, 'He went up, and lay on the child, and put his mouth on his mouth, and his eyes on his eyes, and his hands on his hands. He stretched himself on him; and the flesh of the child grew warm.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  34, 'He went up and lay on the child, and put his mouth on his mouth, and his eyes on his eyes, and his hands on his hands. He stretched himself on him; and the child\'s flesh grew warm.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  35, 'Then he returned, and walked in the house once back and forth; and went up, and stretched himself on him. Then the child sneezed seven times, and the child opened his eyes.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  35, 'Then he returned, and walked in the house once back and forth, then went up and stretched himself out on him. Then the child sneezed seven times, and the child opened his eyes.');
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  37, 'Then she went in, and fell at his feet, and bowed herself to the ground; and she took up her son, and went out.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  37, 'Then she went in, fell at his feet, and bowed herself to the ground; then she picked up her son, and went out.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  38, 'Elisha came again to Gilgal. There was a famine in the land; and the sons of the prophets were sitting before him; and he said to his servant, \"Set on the great pot, and boil stew for the sons of the prophets.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  38, 'Elisha came again to Gilgal. There was a famine in the land; and the sons of the prophets were sitting before him; and he said to his servant, \"Get the large pot, and boil stew for the sons of the prophets.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  39, 'One went out into the field to gather vegetations, and found a wild vine, and gathered of it wild gourds his lap full, and came and shred them into the pot of stew; for they didn\'t recognize them.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  39, 'One went out into the field to gather vegetations, and found a wild vine, and gathered a lap full of wild gourds from it, and came and cut them up into the pot of stew; for they didn\'t recognize them.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  40, 'So they poured out for the men to eat. It happened, as they were eating of the stew, that they cried out, and said, \"Man of God, there is death in the pot!\" They could not eat of it.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  40, 'So they poured out for the men to eat. As they were eating some of the stew, they cried out and said, \"Man of God, there is death in the pot!\" And they could not eat it.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  41, 'But he said, \"Then bring meal.\" He cast it into the pot; and he said, \"Pour out for the people, that they may eat.\" There was no harm in the pot.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  41, 'But he said, \"Then bring meal.\" He threw it into the pot; and he said, \"Serve it to the people, that they may eat.\" And there was nothing harmful in the pot.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  42, 'A man from Baal Shalishah came, and brought the man of God bread of the first fruits, twenty loaves of barley, and fresh ears of grain in his sack. He said, \"Give to the people, that they may eat.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  42, 'A man from Baal Shalishah came, and brought the man of God some bread of the first fruits: twenty loaves of barley and fresh ears of grain in his sack. Elisha said, \"Give to the people, that they may eat.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  43, 'His servant said, \"What, should I set this before a hundred men?\" But he said, \"Give the people, that they may eat; for thus says ForeverOne, \'They will eat, and will have some left over.\'\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  43, 'His servant said, \"What, should I set this before a hundred men?\" But he said, \"Give it to the people, that they may eat; for ForeverOne says, \'They will eat, and will have some left over.\'\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  44, 'So he set it before them, and they ate, and left some of it, according to the word of ForeverOne.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   4,  44, 'So he set it before them and they ate and had some left over, according to ForeverOne\'s word.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   5,   1, 'Now Naaman, captain of the army of the king of Syria, was a great man with his master, and honorable, because by him ForeverOne had given victory to Syria: he was also a mighty man of valor, [but he was] a leper.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   5,   1, 'Now Naaman, captain of the army of the king of Syria, was a great man with his master, and honorable, because by him ForeverOne had given victory to Syria; he was also a mighty man of valor, but he was a leper.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   5,   2, 'The Syrians had gone out in bands, and had brought away captive out of the land of Israel a little maiden; and she waited on Naaman\'s wife.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   5,   2, 'The Syrians had gone out in bands, and had brought away captive out of the land of Israel a little girl, and she waited on Naaman\'s wife.');
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   5,   4, 'Someone went in, and told his lord, saying, \"The maiden who is from the land of Israel said this.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   5,   4, 'Someone went in and told his lord, saying, \"The girl who is from the land of Israel said this.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   5,   5, 'The king of Syria said, \"Go now, and I will send a letter to the king of Israel.\" He departed, and took with him ten talents of silver, and six thousand pieces of gold, and ten changes of clothing.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   5,   5, 'The king of Syria said, \"Go now, and I will send a letter to the king of Israel.\" He departed, and took with him ten talents of silver, six thousand pieces of gold, and ten changes of clothing.');
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   5,   7, 'It happened, when the king of Israel had read the letter, that he tore his clothes, and said, \"Am I God, to kill and to make alive, that this man sends to me to heal a man of his leprosy? But please consider and see how he seeks a quarrel against me.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   5,   7, 'When the king of Israel had read the letter, he tore his clothes and said, \"Am I God, to kill and to make alive, that this man sends to me to heal a man of his leprosy? But please consider and see how he seeks a quarrel against me.\"');
-
-
-
-
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   5,  11, 'But Naaman was angry, and went away, and said, \"Behold, I thought, \'He will surely come out to me, and stand, and call on the name of ForeverOne his God, and wave his hand over the place, and heal the leper.\'');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   5,  11, 'But Naaman was angry, and went away and said, \"Behold, I thought, \'He will surely come out to me, and stand, and call on the name of ForeverOne his God, and wave his hand over the place, and heal the leper.\'');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   5,  12, 'Aren\'t Abanah and Pharpar, the rivers of Damascus, better than all the waters of Israel? Couldn\'t I wash in them, and be clean?\" So he turned and went away in a rage.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   5,  12, 'Aren\'t Abanah and Pharpar, the rivers of Damascus, better than all the waters of Israel? Couldn\'t I wash in them and be clean?\" So he turned and went away in a rage.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   5,  13, 'His servants came near, and spoke to him, and said, \"My father, if the prophet had asked you do some great thing, wouldn\'t you have done it? How much rather then, when he says to you, \'Wash, and be clean?\'\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   5,  13, 'His servants came near and spoke to him, and said, \"My father, if the prophet had asked you do some great thing, wouldn\'t you have done it? How much rather then, when he says to you, \'Wash, and be clean?\'\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   5,  14, 'Then went he down, and dipped [himself] seven times in the Jordan, according to the saying of the man of God; and his flesh was restored like the flesh of a little child, and he was clean.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   5,  14, 'Then went he down and dipped himself seven times in the Jordan, according to the saying of the man of God; and his flesh was restored like the flesh of a little child, and he was clean.');
-
-
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   5,  17, 'Naaman said, \"If not, then, please let there be given to your servant two mules\' burden of earth; for your servant will from now on offer neither burnt offering nor sacrifice to other gods, but to ForeverOne.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   5,  17, 'Naaman said, \"If not, then, please let two mules\' load of earth be given to your servant; for your servant will from now on offer neither burnt offering nor sacrifice to other gods, but to ForeverOne.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   5,  18, 'In this thing may ForeverOne pardon your servan: when my master goes into the house of Rimmon to worship there, and he leans on my hand, and I bow myself in the house of Rimmon. When I bow myself in the house of Rimmon, may ForeverOne pardon your servant in this thing.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   5,  18, 'In this thing may ForeverOne pardon your servant: when my master goes into the house of Rimmon to worship there, and he leans on my hand, and I bow myself in the house of Rimmon. When I bow myself in the house of Rimmon, may ForeverOne pardon your servant in this thing.\"');
-
-
-
-
-
-
-
-
-
-
-
-
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   5,  26, 'He said to him, \"Didn\'t my heart go with you, when the man turned from his chariot to meet you? Is it a time to receive money, and to receive garments, and olive groves and vineyards, and sheep and cattle, and male servants and female servants?');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   5,  26, 'He said to him, \"Didn\'t my heart go with you when the man turned from his chariot to meet you? Is it a time to receive money, and to receive garments, and olive groves and vineyards, and sheep and cattle, and male servants and female servants?');
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,   1, 'The sons of the prophets said to Elisha, \"See now, the place where we dwell before you is too small for us.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,   1, 'The sons of the prophets said to Elisha, \"See now, the place where we live and meet with you is too small for us.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,   2, 'Please let us go to the Jordan, and every man take a beam from there, and let us make us a place there, where we may dwell.\" He answered, \"Go!\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,   2, 'Please let us go to the Jordan, and each man take a beam from there, and let\'s make us a place there, where we may live.\" He answered, \"Go!\"');
-
-
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,   5, 'But as one was felling a beam, the axe head fell into the water. Then he cried, and said, \"Alas, my master! For it was borrowed.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,   5, 'But as one was cutting down a tree, the ax head fell into the water. Then he cried out and said, \"Alas, my master! For it was borrowed.\"');
-
-
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,   8, 'Now the king of Syria was warring against Israel; and he took counsel with his servants, saying, \"My camp will be in such and such a place.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,   8, 'Now the king of Syria was at war against Israel; and he took counsel with his servants, saying, \"My camp will be in such and such a place.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,   9, 'The man of God sent to the king of Israel, saying, \"Beware that you not pass such a place; for the Syrians are coming down there.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,   9, 'The man of God sent to the king of Israel, saying, \"Beware that you not pass this place, for the Syrians are coming down there.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  10, 'The king of Israel sent to the place which the man of God told him and warned him of; and he saved himself there, not once nor twice.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  10, 'The king of Israel sent to the place which the man of God told him and warned him of; and he saved himself there, not once or twice.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  11, 'The heart of the king of Syria was very troubled about this. He called his servants, and said to them, \"Won\'t you show me which of us is for the king of Israel?\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  11, 'The king of Syria\'s heart was very troubled about this. He called his servants, and said to them, \"Won\'t you show me which of us is for the king of Israel?\"');
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  13, 'He said, \"Go and see where he is, that I may send and get him.\" It was told him, saying, \"Behold, he is in Dothan.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  13, 'He said, \"Go and see where he is, that I may send and get him.\" He was told, \"Behold, he is in Dothan.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  14, 'Therefore he sent horses, chariots, and a great army there. They came by night, and surrounded the city.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  14, 'Therefore he sent horses, chariots, and a great army there. They came by night and surrounded the city.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  15, 'When the servant of the man of God had risen early, and gone out, behold, an army with horses and chariots was around the city. His servant said to him, \"Alas, my master! What shall we do?\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  15, 'When the servant of the man of God had risen early and gone out, behold, an army with horses and chariots was around the city. His servant said to him, \"Alas, my master! What shall we do?\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  16, 'He answered, \"Don\'t be afraid; for those who are with us are more than those who are with them.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  16, 'He answered, \"Don\'t be afraid, for those who are with us are more than those who are with them.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  17, 'Elisha prayed, and said, \"ForeverOne, please open his eyes, that he may see.\" ForeverOne opened the eyes of the young man; and he saw: and behold, the mountain was full of horses and chariots of fire around Elisha.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  17, 'Elisha prayed, and said, \"ForeverOne, please open his eyes, that he may see.\" ForeverOne opened the young man\'s eyes, and he saw; and behold, the mountain was full of horses and chariots of fire around Elisha.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  18, 'When they came down to him, Elisha prayed to ForeverOne, and said, \"Please strike this people with blindness.\" He struck them with blindness according to the word of Elisha.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  18, 'When they came down to him, Elisha prayed to ForeverOne, and said, \"Please strike this people with blindness.\" He struck them with blindness according to Elisha\'s word.');
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  20, 'It happened, when they were come into Samaria, that Elisha said, \"ForeverOne, open the eyes of these men, that they may see.\" ForeverOne opened their eyes, and they saw; and behold, they were in the midst of Samaria.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  20, 'When they had come into Samaria, Elisha said, \"ForeverOne, open these men\'s eyes, that they may see.\" ForeverOne opened their eyes, and they saw; and behold, they were in the middle of Samaria.');
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  22, 'He answered, \"You shall not strike them. Would you strike those whom you have taken captive with your sword and with your bow? Set bread and water before them, that they may eat and drink, and go to their master.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  22, 'He answered, \"You shall not strike them. Would you strike those whom you have taken captive with your sword and with your bow? Set bread and water before them, that they may eat and drink, then go to their master.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  23, 'He prepared great feast for them. When they had eaten and drunk, he sent them away, and they went to their master. The bands of Syria stopped raiding the land of Israel.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  23, 'He prepared a great feast for them. After they ate and drank, he sent them away and they went to their master. So the bands of Syria stopped raiding the land of Israel.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  24, 'It happened after this, that Benhadad king of Syria gathered all his army, and went up and besieged Samaria.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  24, 'After this, Benhadad king of Syria gathered all his army, and went up and besieged Samaria.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  25, 'There was a great famine in Samaria. Behold, they besieged it, until a donkey\'s head was sold for eighty pieces of silver, and the fourth part of a kab of dove\'s dung for five pieces of silver.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  25, 'There was a great famine in Samaria. Behold, they besieged it until a donkey\'s head was sold for eighty pieces of silver, and the fourth part of a kab of dove\'s dung for five pieces of silver.');
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  27, 'He said, \"If ForeverOne doesn\'t help you, from where could I help you? From of the threshing floor, or from the winepress?\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  27, 'He said, \"If ForeverOne doesn\'t help you, where could I get help for you? From of the threshing floor, or from the wine press?\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  28, 'The king said to her, \"What ails you?\" She answered, \"This woman said to me, \'Give your son, that we may eat him today, and we will eat my son tomorrow.\'');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  28, 'Then the king asked her, \"What is your problem?\" She answered, \"This woman said to me, \'Give your son, that we may eat him today, and we will eat my son tomorrow.\'');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  29, 'So we boiled my son, and ate him: and I said to her on the next day, \'Give your son, that we may eat him;\' and she has hidden her son.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  29, 'So we boiled my son and ate him; and I said to her on the next day, \'Give up your son, that we may eat him;\' and she has hidden her son.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  30, 'It happened, when the king heard the words of the woman, that he tore his clothes (now he was passing by on the wall); and the people looked, and behold, he had sackcloth underneath on his flesh.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  30, 'When the king heard the words of the woman, he tore his clothes. Now he was passing by on the wall, and the people looked, and behold, he had sackcloth underneath on his body.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  31, 'Then he said, \"God do so to me, and more also, if the head of Elisha the son of Shaphat shall stay on him this day.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   6,  31, 'Then he said, \"God do so to me, and more also, if the head of Elisha the son of Shaphat stays on him today.\"');
-
-
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,   1, 'Elisha said, \"Hear the word of ForeverOne. Thus says ForeverOne, \'Tomorrow about this time a measure of fine flour will be sold for a shekel, and two measures of barley for a shekel, in the gate of Samaria.\'\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,   1, 'Elisha said, \"Hear ForeverOne\'s word. ForeverOne says, \'Tomorrow about this time a seah of fine flour will be sold for a shekel, and two seahs of barley for a shekel, in the gate of Samaria.\'\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,   2, 'Then the captain on whose hand the king leaned answered the man of God, and said, \"Behold, if ForeverOne made windows in heaven, could this thing be?\" He said, \"Behold, you shall see it with your eyes, but shall not eat of it.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,   2, 'Then the captain on whose hand the king leaned answered the man of God, and said, \"Behold, if ForeverOne made windows in heaven, could this thing be?\" He said, \"Behold, you will see it with your eyes, but will not eat of it.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,   3, 'Now there were four leprous men at the entrance of the gate. They said one to another, \"Why do we sit here until we die?');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,   3, 'Now there were four leprous men at the entrance of the gate. They said to one another, \"Why do we sit here until we die?');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,   4, 'If we say, \'We will enter into the city,\' then the famine is in the city, and we shall die there. If we sit still here, we also die. Now therefore come, and let us surrender to the army of the Syrians. If they save us alive, we will live; and if they kill us, we will only die.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,   4, 'If we say, \'We will enter into the city,\' then the famine is in the city, and we will die there. If we sit still here, we also die. Now therefore come, and let\'s surrender to the army of the Syrians. If they save us alive, we will live; and if they kill us, we will only die.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,   5, 'They rose up in the twilight, to go to the camp of the Syrians. When they had come to the outermost part of the camp of the Syrians, behold, there was no man there.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,   5, 'They rose up in the twilight to go to the camp of the Syrians. When they had come to the outermost part of the camp of the Syrians, behold, no man was there.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,   6, 'For the Lord had made the army of the Syrians to hear a noise of chariots, and a noise of horses, even the noise of a great army: and they said one to another, Behold, the king of Israel has hired against us the kings of the Hittites, and the kings of the Egyptians, to come on us.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,   6, 'For the Lord had made the army of the Syrians to hear the sound of chariots and the sound of horses, even the noise of a great army; and they said to one another, \"Behold, the king of Israel has hired against us the kings of the Hittites and the kings of the Egyptians to attack us.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,   7, 'Therefore they arose and fled in the twilight, and left their tents, and their horses, and their donkeys, even the camp as it was, and fled for their life.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,   7, 'Therefore they arose and fled in the twilight, and left their tents, their horses, and their donkeys, even the camp as it was, and fled for their life.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,   8, 'When these lepers came to the outermost part of the camp, they went into one tent, and ate and drink, and carried there silver, and gold, and clothing, and went and hid it. Then they came back, and entered into another tent, and carried there also, and went and hid it.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,   8, 'When these lepers came to the outermost part of the camp, they went into one tent, and ate and drank, then carried away silver, gold, and clothing and went and hid it. Then they came back, and entered into another tent and carried things from there also, and went and hid them.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,   9, 'Then they said one to another, \"We aren\'t doing right. This day is a day of good news, and we keep silent. If we wait until the morning light, punishment will overtake us. Now therefore come, let us go and tell the king\'s household.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,   9, 'Then they said to one another, \"We aren\'t doing right. Today is a day of good news, and we keep silent. If we wait until the morning light, punishment will overtake us. Now therefore come, let\'s go and tell the king\'s household.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,  10, 'So they came and called to the porter of the city; and they told them, saying, \"We came to the camp of the Syrians, and, behold, there was no man there, neither voice of man, but the horses tied, and the donkeys tied, and the tents as they were.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,  10, 'So they came and called to the city gatekeepers; and they told them, \"We came to the camp of the Syrians, and, behold, there was no man there, not even a man\'s voice, but the horses tied, and the donkeys tied, and the tents as they were.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,  11, 'He called the porters; and they told it to the king\'s household within.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,  11, 'Then the gatekeepers called out and told it to the king\'s household within.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,  12, 'The king arose in the night, and said to his servants, \"I will now show you what the Syrians have done to us. They know that we are hungry. Therefore are they gone out of the camp to hide themselves in the field, saying, \'When they come out of the city, we shall take them alive, and get into the city.\'\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,  12, 'The king arose in the night, and said to his servants, \"I will now show you what the Syrians have done to us. They know that we are hungry. Therefore they have gone out of the camp to hide themselves in the field, saying, \'When they come out of the city, we shall take them alive, and get into the city.\'\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,  13, 'One of his servants answered, \"Please let some take five of the horses that remain, which are left in the city. Behold, they are like all the multitude of Israel who are left in it. Behold, they are like all the multitude of Israel who are consumed. Let us send and see.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,  13, 'One of his servants answered, \"Please let some people take five of the horses that remain, which are left in the city. Behold, they are like all the multitude of Israel who are left in it. Behold, they are like all the multitude of Israel who are consumed. Let\'s send and see.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,  14, 'They took therefore two chariots with horses; and the king sent after the army of the Syrians, saying, \"Go and see.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,  14, 'Therefore they took two chariots with horses; and the king sent them out to the Syrian army, saying, \"Go and see.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,  15, 'They went after them to the Jordan; and behold, all the way was full of garments and vessels, which the Syrians had cast away in their haste. The messengers returned, and told the king.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,  15, 'They went after them to the Jordan; and behold, all the path was full of garments and equipment which the Syrians had cast away in their haste. The messengers returned and told the king.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,  16, 'The people went out, and plundered the camp of the Syrians. So a measure of fine flour was [sold] for a shekel, and two measures of barley for a shekel, according to the word of ForeverOne.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,  16, 'The people went out and plundered the camp of the Syrians. So a seah of fine flour was sold for a shekel, and two measures of barley for a shekel, according to ForeverOne\'s word.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,  17, 'The king appointed the captain on whose hand he leaned to be in charge of the gate: and the people trod on him in the gate, and he died as the man of God had said, who spoke when the king came down to him.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,  17, 'The king had appointed the captain on whose hand he leaned to be in charge of the gate; and the people trampled over him in the gate, and he died as the man of God had said, who spoke when the king came down to him.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,  18, 'It happened, as the man of God had spoken to the king, saying, \"Two measures of barley for a shekel, and a measure of fine flour for a shekel, shall be tomorrow about this time in the gate of Samaria;\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,  18, 'It happened as the man of God had spoken to the king, saying, \"Two seahs of barley for a shekel, and a seah of fine flour for a shekel, shall be tomorrow about this time in the gate of Samaria;\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,  19, 'and that captain answered the man of God, and said, \"Now, behold, if ForeverOne should make windows in heaven, might such a thing be?\" and he said, \"Behold, you shall see it with your eyes, but shall not eat of it.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,  19, 'and that captain answered the man of God, and said, \"Now, behold, if ForeverOne made windows in heaven, might such a thing be?\" and he said, \"Behold, you will see it with your eyes, but will not eat of it.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,  20, 'It happened like that to him; for the people trod on him in the gate, and he died.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   7,  20, 'It happened like that to him, for the people trampled over him in the gate, and he died.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,   1, 'Now Elisha had spoken to the woman, whose son he had restored to life, saying, \"Arise, and go, you and your household, and stay for a while wherever you can; for ForeverOne has called for a famine. It shall also come on the land seven years.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,   1, 'Now Elisha had spoken to the woman whose son he had restored to life, saying, \"Arise, and go, you and your household, and stay for a while wherever you can; for ForeverOne has called for a famine. It will also come on the land for seven years.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,   2, 'The woman arose, and did according to the word of the man of God. She went with her household, and lived in the land of the Philistines seven years.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,   2, 'The woman arose, and did according to the man of God\'s word. She went with her household, and lived in the land of the Philistines for seven years.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,   3, 'It happened at the seven years\' end, that the woman returned out of the land of the Philistines. Then she went forth to cry to the king for her house and for her land.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,   3, 'At the end of seven years, the woman returned from the land of the Philistines. Then she went out to beg the king for her house and for her land.');
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,   5, 'It happened, as he was telling the king how he had restored to life him who was dead, that behold, the woman, whose son he had restored to life, cried to the king for her house and for her land. Gehazi said, \"My lord, O king, this is the woman, and this is her son, whom Elisha restored to life.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,   5, 'As he was telling the king how he had restored to life him who was dead, behold, the woman whose son he had restored to life begged the king for her house and for her land. Gehazi said, \"My lord, O king, this is the woman, and this is her son, whom Elisha restored to life.\"');
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,   7, 'Elisha came to Damascus; and Benhadad the king of Syria was sick. It was told him, saying, \"The man of God has come here.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,   7, 'Elisha came to Damascus; and Benhadad the king of Syria was sick. He was told, \"The man of God has come here.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,   8, 'The king said to Hazael, \"Take a present in your hand, and go, meet the man of God, and inquire of ForeverOne by him, saying, \'Will I recover from this sickness?\'\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,   8, 'The king said to Hazael, \"Take a present in your hand, and go meet the man of God, and inquire of ForeverOne by him, saying, \'Will I recover from this sickness?\'\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,   9, 'So Hazael went to meet him, and took a present with him, even of every good thing of Damascus, forty camels\' burden, and came and stood before him, and said, \"Your son Benhadad king of Syria has sent me to you, saying, \'Will I recover from this sickness?\'\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,   9, 'So Hazael went to meet him and took a present with him, even of every good thing of Damascus, forty camels\' burden, and came and stood before him and said, \"Your son Benhadad king of Syria has sent me to you, saying, \'Will I recover from this sickness?\'\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,  10, 'Elisha said to him, \"Go, tell him, \'You shall surely recover;\' however ForeverOne has shown me that he shall surely die.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,  10, 'Elisha said to him, \"Go, tell him, \'You will surely recover;\' however ForeverOne has shown me that he will surely die.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,  11, 'He settled his gaze steadfastly [on him], until he was ashamed. Then the man of God wept.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,  11, 'He settled his gaze steadfastly on him, until he was ashamed. Then the man of God wept.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,  12, 'Hazael said, \"Why do you weep, my lord?\" He answered, \"Because I know the evil that you will do to the children of Israel. You will set their strongholds on fire, and you will kill their young men with the sword, and will dash in pieces their little ones, and rip up their women with child.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,  12, 'Hazael said, \"Why do you weep, my lord?\" He answered, \"Because I know the evil that you will do to the children of Israel. You will set their strongholds on fire, and you will kill their young men with the sword, and will dash their little ones in pieces, and rip up their pregnant women.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,  13, 'Hazael said, \"But what is your servant, who is but a dog, that he should do this great thing?\" Elisha answered, \"ForeverOne has shown me that you will be king over Syria.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,  13, 'Hazael said, \"But what is your servant, who is but a dog, that he could do this great thing?\" Elisha answered, \"ForeverOne has shown me that you will be king over Syria.\"');
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,  15, 'It happened on the next day, that he took a thick cloth, dipped it in water, and spread it on his face, so that he died. Then Hazael reigned in his place.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,  15, 'On the next day, he took a thick cloth, dipped it in water, and spread it on the king\'s face, so that he died. Then Hazael reigned in his place.');
-
-
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,  18, 'He walked in the way of the kings of Israel, as did the house of Ahab; for he had the daughter of Ahab as wife. He did that which was evil in the sight of ForeverOne.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,  18, 'He walked in the way of the kings of Israel, as did Ahab\'s house, for he married Ahab\'s daughter. He did that which was evil in ForeverOne\'s sight.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,  19, 'However ForeverOne would not destroy Judah, for David his servant\'s sake, as he promised him to give to him a lamp for his children always.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,  19, 'However, ForeverOne would not destroy Judah, for David his servant\'s sake, as he promised him to give to him a lamp for his children always.');
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,  21, 'Then Joram passed over to Zair, and all his chariots with him: and he rose up by night, and struck the Edomites who surrounded him, and the captains of the chariots; and the people fled to their tents.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,  21, 'Then Joram crossed over to Zair, and all his chariots with him; and he rose up by night and struck the Edomites who surrounded him with the captains of the chariots; and the people fled to their tents.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,  22, 'So Edom revolted from under the hand of Judah to this day. Then did Libnah revolt at the same time.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,  22, 'So Edom revolted from under the hand of Judah to this day. Then Libnah revolted at the same time.');
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,  24, 'Joram slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in the city of David; and Ahaziah his son reigned in his place.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,  24, 'Joram slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in David\'s city; and Ahaziah his son reigned in his place.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,  25, 'In the twelfth year of Joram the son of Ahab king of Israel did Ahaziah the son of Jehoram king of Judah begin to reign.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,  25, 'In the twelfth year of Joram the son of Ahab king of Israel, Ahaziah the son of Jehoram king of Judah began to reign.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,  26, 'Twenty-two years old was Ahaziah when he began to reign; and he reigned one year in Jerusalem. His mother\'s name was Athaliah the daughter of Omri king of Israel.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,  26, 'Ahaziah was twenty-two years old when he began to reign; and he reigned one year in Jerusalem. His mother\'s name was Athaliah the daughter of Omri king of Israel.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,  27, 'He walked in the way of the house of Ahab, and did that which was evil in the sight of ForeverOne, as did the house of Ahab; for he was the son-in-law of the house of Ahab.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,  27, 'He walked in the way of Ahab\'s house and did that which was evil in ForeverOne\'s sight, as did Ahab\'s house, for he was the son-in-law of Ahab\'s house.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,  28, 'He went with Joram the son of Ahab to war against Hazael king of Syria at Ramoth Gilead: and the Syrians wounded Joram.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,  28, 'He went with Joram the son of Ahab to war against Hazael king of Syria at Ramoth Gilead, and the Syrians wounded Joram.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,  29, 'King Joram returned to be healed in Jezreel of the wounds which the Syrians had given him at Ramah, when he fought against Hazael king of Syria. Ahaziah the son of Jehoram king of Judah went down to see Joram the son of Ahab in Jezreel, because he was sick.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   8,  29, 'King Joram returned to be healed in Jezreel from the wounds which the Syrians had given him at Ramah, when he fought against Hazael king of Syria. Ahaziah the son of Jehoram, king of Judah, went down to see Joram the son of Ahab in Jezreel, because he was sick.');
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,   2, 'When you come there, find Jehu the son of Jehoshaphat the son of Nimshi, and go in, and make him arise up from among his brothers, and carry him to an inner room.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,   2, 'When you come there, find Jehu the son of Jehoshaphat the son of Nimshi, and go in and make him rise up from among his brothers, and take him to an inner room.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,   3, 'Then take the vial of oil, and pour it on his head, and say, \'Thus says ForeverOne, \"I have anointed you king over Israel.\"\' Then open the door, flee, and don\'t wait.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,   3, 'Then take the vial of oil, and pour it on his head, and say, \'ForeverOne says, \"I have anointed you king over Israel.\"\' Then open the door, flee, and don\'t wait.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,   4, 'So the young man, even the young man the prophet, went to Ramoth Gilead.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,   4, 'So the young man, the young prophet, went to Ramoth Gilead.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,   5, 'When he came, behold, the captains of the army were sitting. Then he said, \"I have a message for you, captain.\" Jehu said, \"To which of us all?\" He said, \"To you, O captain.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,   5, 'When he came, behold, the captains of the army were sitting. Then he said, \"I have a message for you, captain.\" Jehu said, \"To which one of us?\" He said, \"To you, O captain.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,   6, 'He arose, and went into the house. Then he poured the oil on his head, and said to him, \"Thus says ForeverOne, the God of Israel, \'I have anointed you king over the people of ForeverOne, even over Israel.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,   6, 'He arose, and went into the house. Then he poured the oil on his head, and said to him, \"ForeverOne, the God of Israel, says, \'I have anointed you king over the people of ForeverOne, even over Israel.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,   7, 'You shall strike the house of Ahab your master, that I may avenge the blood of my servants the prophets, and the blood of all the servants of ForeverOne, at the hand of Jezebel.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,   7, 'You must strike your master Ahab\'s house, that I may avenge the blood of my servants the prophets, and the blood of all the servants of ForeverOne, at the hand of Jezebel.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,   8, 'For the whole house of Ahab shall perish. I will cut off from Ahab everyone who urinates against a wall, both him who is shut up and him who is left at large in Israel.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,   8, 'For the whole house of Ahab will perish. I will cut off from Ahab everyone who urinates against a wall, both him who is shut up and him who is left at large in Israel.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,   9, 'I will make the house of Ahab like the house of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, and like the house of Baasha the son of Ahijah.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,   9, 'I will make Ahab\'s house like the house of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, and like the house of Baasha the son of Ahijah.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  10, 'The dogs will eat Jezebel on the plot of ground of Jezreel, and there shall be none to bury her.\'\" He opened the door, and fled.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  10, 'The dogs will eat Jezebel on the plot of ground of Jezreel, and there shall be no one to bury her.\'\" Then he opened the door and fled.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  11, 'Then Jehu came forth to the servants of his lord: and one said to him, \"Is all well? Why did this mad fellow come to you?\" He said to them, \"You know the man and what his talk was.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  11, 'When Jehu came out to the servants of his lord and one said to him, \"Is all well? Why did this madman come to you?\" He said to them, \"You know the man and how he talks.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  12, 'They said, \"That is a lie. Tell us now.\" He said, \"He said to me, \'Thus says ForeverOne, I have anointed you king over Israel.\'\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  12, 'They said, \"That is a lie. Tell us now.\" He said, \"He said to me, \'ForeverOne says, I have anointed you king over Israel.\'\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  13, 'Then they hurried, and took every man his garment, and put it under him on the top of the stairs, and blew the trumpet, saying, \"Jehu is king.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  13, 'Then they hurried, and each man took his cloak, and put it under him on the top of the stairs, and blew the trumpet, saying, \"Jehu is king.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  14, 'So Jehu the son of Jehoshaphat the son of Nimshi conspired against Joram. (Now Joram was keeping Ramoth Gilead, he and all Israel, because of Hazael king of Syria;');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  14, 'So Jehu the son of Jehoshaphat the son of Nimshi conspired against Joram. (Now Joram was defending Ramoth Gilead, he and all Israel, because of Hazael king of Syria;');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  15, 'but king Joram was returned to be healed in Jezreel of the wounds which the Syrians had given him, when he fought with Hazael king of Syria.) Jehu said, \"If this is your thinking, then let no one escape and go out of the city, to go to tell it in Jezreel.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  15, 'but King Joram had returned to be healed in Jezreel of the wounds which the Syrians had given him when he fought with Hazael king of Syria.) Jehu said, \"If this is your thinking, then let no one escape and go out of the city to go to tell it in Jezreel.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  16, 'So Jehu rode in a chariot, and went to Jezreel; for Joram lay there. Ahaziah king of Judah had come down to see Joram.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  16, 'So Jehu rode in a chariot and went to Jezreel, for Joram lay there. Ahaziah king of Judah had come down to see Joram.');
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  18, 'So there went one on horseback to meet him, and said, \"Thus says the king, \'Is it peace?\'\" Jehu said, \"What do you have to do with peace? Fall in behind me!\" The watchman said, \"The messenger came to them, but he isn\'t coming back.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  18, 'So one went on horseback to meet him, and said, \"the king says, \'Is it peace?\'\" Jehu said, \"What do you have to do with peace? Fall in behind me!\" The watchman said, \"The messenger came to them, but he isn\'t coming back.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  19, 'Then he sent out a second on horseback, who came to them, and said, \"Thus says the king, \'Is it peace?\'\" Jehu answered, \"What do you have to do with peace? Fall in behind me!\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  19, 'Then he sent out a second on horseback, who came to them and said, \"The king says, \'Is it peace?\'\" Jehu answered, \"What do you have to do with peace? Fall in behind me!\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  20, 'The watchman said, \"He came to them, and isn\'t coming back. The driving is like the driving of Jehu the son of Nimshi; for he drives furiously.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  20, 'The watchman said, \"He came to them, and isn\'t coming back. The driving is like the driving of Jehu the son of Nimshi, for he drives furiously.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  21, 'Joram said, \"Get ready!\" They got his chariot ready. Joram king of Israel and Ahaziah king of Judah went out, each in his chariot, and they went out to meet Jehu, and found him in the portion of Naboth the Jezreelite.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  21, 'Joram said, \"Get ready!\" They got his chariot ready. Then Joram king of Israel and Ahaziah king of Judah went out, each in his chariot; and they went out to meet Jehu, and found him on Naboth the Jezreelite\'s land.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  22, 'It happened, when Joram saw Jehu, that he said, \"Is it peace, Jehu?\" He answered, \"What peace, so long as the prostitution of your mother Jezebel and her witchcraft abound?\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  22, 'When Joram saw Jehu, he said, \"Is it peace, Jehu?\" He answered, \"What peace, so long as the prostitution of your mother Jezebel and her witchcraft abound?\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  23, 'Joram turned his hands, and fled, and said to Ahaziah, \"There is treason, Ahaziah!\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  23, 'Joram turned his hands and fled, and said to Ahaziah, \"This is treason, Ahaziah!\"');
-
-
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  26, '\'Surely I have seen yesterday the blood of Naboth, and the blood of his sons,\' says ForeverOne; \'and I will repay you in this plot of ground,\' says ForeverOne. Now therefore take and cast him onto the plot of ground, according to the word of ForeverOne.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  26, '\'Surely I have seen yesterday the blood of Naboth, and the blood of his sons,\' says ForeverOne; \'and I will repay you in this plot of ground,\' says ForeverOne. Now therefore take and cast him onto the plot of ground, according to ForeverOne\'s word.\"');
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  28, 'His servants carried him in a chariot to Jerusalem, and buried him in his tomb with his fathers in the city of David.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  28, 'His servants carried him in a chariot to Jerusalem, and buried him in his tomb with his fathers in David\'s city.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  29, 'In the eleventh year of Joram the son of Ahab began Ahaziah to reign over Judah.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  29, 'In the eleventh year of Joram the son of Ahab, Ahaziah began to reign over Judah.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  30, 'When Jehu was come to Jezreel, Jezebel heard of it; and she painted her eyes, and attired her head, and looked out at the window.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  30, 'When Jehu had come to Jezreel, Jezebel heard of it; and she painted her eyes, and adorned her head, and looked out at the window.');
-
-
-
-
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  34, 'When he was come in, he ate and drink; and he said, \"See now to this cursed woman, and bury her; for she is a king\'s daughter.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  34, 'When he had come in, he ate and drank. Then he said, \"See now to this cursed woman, and bury her; for she is a king\'s daughter.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  35, 'They went to bury her; but they found no more of her than the skull, and the feet, and the palms of her hands.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  35, 'They went to bury her, but they found no more of her than the skull, the feet, and the palms of her hands.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  36, 'Therefore they came back, and told him. He said, \"This is the word of ForeverOne, which he spoke by his servant Elijah the Tishbite, saying, \'The dogs will eat the flesh of Jezebel on the plot of Jezreel,');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  36, 'Therefore they came back, and told him. He said, \"This is ForeverOne\'s word, which he spoke by his servant Elijah the Tishbite, saying, \'The dogs will eat the flesh of Jezebel on the plot of Jezreel,');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  37, 'and the body of Jezebel shall be as dung on the face of the field in the portion of Jezreel, so that they shall not say, \"This is Jezebel.\"\'\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',   9,  37, 'and the body of Jezebel will be as dung on the surface of the field on Jezreel\'s land, so that they won\'t say, \"This is Jezebel.\"\'\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',  10,   1, 'Now Ahab had seventy sons in Samaria. Jehu wrote letters, and sent to Samaria, to the rulers of Jezreel, even the elders, and to those who brought up [the sons of] Ahab, saying,');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',  10,   1, 'Now Ahab had seventy sons in Samaria. Jehu wrote letters and sent them to Samaria, to the rulers of Jezreel, even the elders, and to those who brought up Ahab\'s sons, saying,');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',  10,   2, '\"Now as soon as this letter comes to you, since your master\'s sons are with you, and there are with you chariots and horses, a fortified city also, and armor.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',  10,   2, '\"Now as soon as this letter comes to you, since your master\'s sons are with you, and you have chariots and horses, a fortified city also, and armor,');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',  10,   3, 'Select the best and fittest of your master\'s sons, set him on his father\'s throne, and fight for your master\'s house.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',  10,   3, 'select the best and fittest of your master\'s sons, set him on his father\'s throne, and fight for your master\'s house.\"');
-
-
-
-
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',  10,   6, 'Then he wrote a letter the second time to them, saying, \"If you are on my side, and if you will listen to my voice, take the heads of the men your master\'s sons, and come to me to Jezreel by tomorrow this time.\" Now the king\'s sons, being seventy persons, were with the great men of the city, who brought them up.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',  10,   6, 'Then he wrote a letter the second time to them, saying, \"If you are on my side, and if you will listen to my voice, take the heads of the men who are your master\'s sons, and come to me to Jezreel by tomorrow this time.\" Now the king\'s sons, being seventy persons, were with the great men of the city, who brought them up.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',  10,   7, 'It happened, when the letter came to them, that they took the king\'s sons, and killed them, even seventy persons, and put their heads in baskets, and sent them to him to Jezreel.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',  10,   7, 'When the letter came to them, they took the king\'s sons and killed them, even seventy people, and put their heads in baskets, and sent them to him to Jezreel.');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',  10,   8, 'A messenger came, and told him, \"They have brought the heads of the king\'s sons.\" He said, \"Lay them in two heaps at the entrance of the gate until the morning.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',  10,   8, 'A messenger came and told him, \"They have brought the heads of the king\'s sons.\" He said, \"Lay them in two heaps at the entrance of the gate until the morning.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',  10,   9, 'It happened in the morning, that he went out, and stood, and said to all the people, \"You are righteous. Behold, I conspired against my master, and killed him; but who struck all these?');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',  10,   9, 'In the morning, he went out and stood, and said to all the people, \"You are righteous. Behold, I conspired against my master and killed him, but who killed all these?');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',  10,  10, 'Know now that nothing shall fall to the earth of the word of ForeverOne, which ForeverOne spoke concerning the house of Ahab. For ForeverOne has done that which he spoke by his servant Elijah.\"');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',  10,  10, 'Know now that nothing will fall to the earth of ForeverOne\'s word, which ForeverOne spoke concerning Ahab\'s house. For ForeverOne has done that which he spoke by his servant Elijah.\"');
INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',  10,  11, 'So Jehu struck all that remained of the house of Ahab in Jezreel, with all his great men, his familiar friends, and his priests, until he left him none remaining.');
--INSERT INTO `verses` (`bookCode`, `chapter`, `verseNumber`, `verseText`) VALUES ('2KI',  10,  11, 'So Jehu struck all that remained of Ahab\'s house in Jezreel, with all his great men, his familiar friends, and his priests, until he left him no one remaining.');
